<title>JAPAN: Toho Mutual says needs more time to cut bad loans.</title>
<headline>Toho Mutual says needs more time to cut bad loans.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1996-11-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Toho Mutual Life Insurance Co said on Thursday that it would take a few more years to reduce its bad loans to a manageable level.</p>
<p>In conjunction with its earnings announcement for the first half of the 1996/97 business year, the company said that 40 billion yen worth of its loans to affiliated non-bank financial institutions had either been forgiven or had had their interest rates reduced.</p>
</text>
